---
const services = [
  {
    id: 'onboarding',
    title: 'Developer Onboarding Optimization',
    description:
      'Turn your onboarding process into a quick win. We redesign first-run experiences that convert curious developers into active builders.',
    icon: `<svg class="w-8 h-8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15.59 14.37a6 6 0 0 1-5.84 7.38v-4.8m5.84-2.58a14.98 14.98 0 0 0 6.16-12.12A14.98 14.98 0 0 0 9.631 8.41m5.96 5.96a14.926 14.926 0 0 1-5.841 2.58m-.119-8.54a6 6 0 0 0-7.381 5.84h4.8m2.581-5.84a14.927 14.927 0 0 0-2.58 5.84m2.699 2.7c-.103.021-.207.041-.311.06a15.09 15.09 0 0 1-2.448-2.448 14.9 14.9 0 0 1 .06-.312m-2.24 2.39a4.493 4.493 0 0 0-1.757 4.306 4.493 4.493 0 0 0 4.306-1.758M16.5 9a1.5 1.5 0 1 1-3 0 1.5 1.5 0 0 1 3 0Z" /></svg>`,
    fullContent: `
      <p class="text-text-primary mb-4">
        <strong>The first 30 minutes decide everything.</strong> When a developer lands on your docs,
        they're asking one question: "Can I ship something with this?" Most onboarding flows fail
        because they explain architecture before demonstrating the fun stuff.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
        We audit your entire developer journey — from landing page to first successful API call
        — and fix the friction points that kill adoption. Time-to-Hello-World analysis. Error
        message digging. Cognitive load reduction. Environment setup elimination.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-secondary">
        We cut onboarding time from hours to minutes for blockchain projects where "run this
        setup steps" was considered acceptable.
      </p>
    `,
  },
  {
    id: 'documentation',
    title: 'Technical Documentation Audits',
    description:
      'AI agents read your docs before developers do. We audit and restructure documentation to be machine-parseable, LLM-friendly, and human-clear.',
    icon: `<svg class="w-8 h-8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 14.25v-2.625a3.375 3.375 0 0 0-3.375-3.375h-1.5A1.125 1.125 0 0 1 13.5 7.125v-1.5a3.375 3.375 0 0 0-3.375-3.375H8.25m5.231 13.481L15 17.25m-4.5-15H5.625c-.621 0-1.125.504-1.125 1.125v16.5c0 .621.504 1.125 1.125 1.125h12.75c.621 0 1.125-.504 1.125-1.125V11.25a9 9 0 0 0-9-9Zm3.75 11.625a2.625 2.625 0 1 1-5.25 0 2.625 2.625 0 0 1 5.25 0Z" /></svg>`,
    fullContent: `
      <p class="text-text-primary mb-4">
        <strong>Your docs have drifted from reality.</strong> Not intentionally. But that tutorial
        from 18 months ago? The API reference that's three versions behind? They're actively driving
        developers away.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
        We run systematic audits that surface accuracy decay, discovery failures,
        maintainability gaps, and AI-readability issues. Because AI agents read your docs before
        developers do — and most docs fail both audiences.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-secondary">
        The deliverable isn't a PDF you'll ignore. It's a prioritized fix list with estimated
        impact.
      </p>
    `,
  },
  {
    id: 'hackathons',
    title: 'Hackathon Operations',
    description:
      'Our signature model. End-to-end hackathon design and execution — from challenge crafting to judging to winner follow-up. High signal, zero noise.',
    icon: `<svg class="w-8 h-8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M16.5 18.75h-9m9 0a3 3 0 0 1 3 3h-15a3 3 0 0 1 3-3m9 0v-3.375c0-.621-.503-1.125-1.125-1.125h-.871M7.5 18.75v-3.375c0-.621.504-1.125 1.125-1.125h.872m5.007 0H9.497m5.007 0a7.454 7.454 0 0 1-.982-3.172M9.497 14.25a7.454 7.454 0 0 0 .981-3.172M5.25 4.236c-.982.143-1.954.317-2.916.52A6.003 6.003 0 0 0 7.73 9.728M5.25 4.236V4.5c0 2.108.966 3.99 2.48 5.228M5.25 4.236V2.721C7.456 2.41 9.71 2.25 12 2.25c2.291 0 4.545.16 6.75.47v1.516M7.73 9.728a6.726 6.726 0 0 0 2.748 1.35m8.272-6.842V4.5c0 2.108-.966 3.99-2.48 5.228m2.48-5.492a46.32 46.32 0 0 1 2.916.52 6.003 6.003 0 0 1-5.395 4.972m0 0a6.726 6.726 0 0 1-2.749 1.35m0 0a6.772 6.772 0 0 1-3.044 0" /></svg>`,
    fullContent: `
      <p class="text-text-primary mb-4">
        <strong>Our signature battle-tested hackathon model.</strong> We've run presence at ETHBelgrade,
        ETHRome, ETHLisbon, TUM Blockchain, and global online hackathons. Not as sponsors who show
        up with swag. As a coordinated team of operators who drive measurable developer adoption.
      </p>
      <div class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
        <p class="mb-2">Our hackathon model:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 ml-2">
          <li>Pre-event developer activation — workshops, meetups, content</li>
          <li>On-site technical support — engineers who debug your stack at 2am</li>
          <li>
            Project Clinic workshops — helping hackers strengthen product, UX, and target
            audience
          </li>
          <li>
            Real-time feedback loops — we surface onboarding and tooling issues while the event
            runs
          </li>
          <li>
            Post-event reporting — actual metrics: submissions, completion rates, sentiment,
            conversion
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <p class="text-text-secondary">
        At ETHBelgrade, we captured <strong>25.6% market share</strong> against native Ethereum tracks.
        That doesn't happen with a booth and some stickers.
      </p>
    `,
  },
  {
    id: 'incubation',
    title: 'Post-Hackathon Support',
    description:
      'Hackathon winners disappear. We run team incubation programs that turn weekend projects into production deployments and retained developers.',
    icon: `<svg class="w-8 h-8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M18 18.72a9.094 9.094 0 0 0 3.741-.479 3 3 0 0 0-4.682-2.72m.94 3.198.001.031c0 .225-.012.447-.037.666A11.944 11.944 0 0 1 12 21c-2.17 0-4.207-.576-5.963-1.584A6.062 6.062 0 0 1 6 18.719m12 0a5.971 5.971 0 0 0-.941-3.197m0 0A5.995 5.995 0 0 0 12 12.75a5.995 5.995 0 0 0-5.058 2.772m0 0a3 3 0 0 0-4.681 2.72 8.986 8.986 0 0 0 3.74.477m.94-3.197a5.971 5.971 0 0 0-.94 3.197M15 6.75a3 3 0 1 1-6 0 3 3 0 0 1 6 0Zm6 3a2.25 2.25 0 1 1-4.5 0 2.25 2.25 0 0 1 4.5 0Zm-13.5 0a2.25 2.25 0 1 1-4.5 0 2.25 2.25 0 0 1 4.5 0Z" /></svg>`,
    fullContent: `
      <p class="text-text-primary mb-4">
        <strong>Hackathons produce prototypes. We help them become products.</strong> The dirty secret
        of hackathons: over 90% of projects end right there. Not because the ideas were bad, but because
        nobody helped the teams navigate what comes next.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
        We provide structured post-hackathon support: technical viability assessment,
        architecture guidance, ecosystem integration, and grant/funding preparation. For
        ecosystems running hackathons, this is how you convert one-time participants into
        long-term builders.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-secondary">
        One ETHBelgrade participant was selected for Polkadot Blockchain Academy in Bali and
        started an interview process at Parity. That's the pipeline.
      </p>
    `,
  },
  {
    id: 'devrel-strategy',
    title: 'Ecosystem DevRel Strategy',
    description:
      'Beyond content calendars. We build DevRel programs with measurable outcomes — developer activation, retention metrics, and community health indicators.',
    icon: `<svg class="w-8 h-8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3.75 3v11.25A2.25 2.25 0 0 0 6 16.5h2.25M3.75 3h-1.5m1.5 0h16.5m0 0h1.5m-1.5 0v11.25A2.25 2.25 0 0 1 18 16.5h-2.25m-7.5 0h7.5m-7.5 0-1 3m8.5-3 1 3m0 0 .5 1.5m-.5-1.5h-9.5m0 0-.5 1.5m.75-9 3-3 2.148 2.148A12.061 12.061 0 0 1 16.5 7.605" /></svg>`,
    fullContent: `
      <p class="text-text-primary mb-4">
        <strong>Beyond content calendars.</strong> Most DevRel programs measure activity instead of
        outcomes. Posts published. Events attended. Followers gained. None of that tells you if developers
        are actually building.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
        We build DevRel programs with measurable outcomes — developer activation, retention
        metrics, and community health indicators. We map and foster existing initiatives,
        establish coordination across teams, and create governance mechanisms.
      </p>
    `,
  },
  {
    id: 'education',
    title: 'Blockchain Education & Consulting',
    description:
      'Technical workshops on smart contracts, runtime architecture, and AI agents. Strategic consulting to help protocols focus developer efforts for maximum impact.',
    icon: `<svg class="w-8 h-8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4.26 10.147a60.438 60.438 0 0 0-.491 6.347A48.62 48.62 0 0 1 12 20.904a48.62 48.62 0 0 1 8.232-4.41 60.46 60.46 0 0 0-.491-6.347m-15.482 0a50.636 50.636 0 0 0-2.658-.813A59.906 59.906 0 0 1 12 3.493a59.903 59.903 0 0 1 10.399 5.84c-.896.248-1.783.52-2.658.814m-15.482 0A50.717 50.717 0 0 1 12 13.489a50.702 50.702 0 0 1 7.74-3.342M6.75 15a.75.75 0 1 0 0-1.5.75.75 0 0 0 0 1.5Zm0 0v-3.675A55.378 55.378 0 0 1 12 8.443m-7.007 11.55A5.981 5.981 0 0 0 6.75 15.75v-1.5" /></svg>`,
    fullContent: `
      <p class="text-text-primary mb-4">
        <strong>Teaching what we've learned.</strong> We offer technical workshops on smart contract
        development, runtime architecture, data indexing, and AI agent integration. We also consult
        on ecosystem strategy — helping protocols figure out where to focus their developer efforts
        for maximum impact.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-secondary">
        Whether it's a 2-hour workshop at a conference or a multi-week training program for your
        team, we teach what actually works in production.
      </p>
    `,
  },
];
---

<section id="services" class="pt-12 pb-12 overflow-hidden bg-bg-primary">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6">
    <h2 data-animate class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold font-coconat text-center relative z-20">
      Our Services
    </h2>
    <p data-animate data-delay="100" class="mt-4 text-center text-text-secondary relative z-20">
      Full-stack DevRel. From "getting started" to production deployment.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-16 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      {
        services.map((service, i) => (
          <>
            <button
              data-animate
              data-delay={150 + i * 50}
              data-service-trigger={service.id}
              class="service-card p-6 rounded-xl border-l-4 border-l-brand-500 border-t border-t-brand-500 border-r border-r-brand-500 border-b border-b-brand-500 transition-all group relative z-10 text-left w-full cursor-pointer"
              aria-label={`Learn more about ${service.title}`}
            >
              <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
                {/* eslint-disable-next-line astro/no-set-html-directive -- Safe: hardcoded static SVG from frontmatter */}
                <div class="service-icon text-accent flex-shrink-0" set:html={service.icon} />
                <div>
                  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold font-coconat text-text-primary group-hover:text-accent transition-colors">
                    {service.title}
                  </h3>
                  <p class="mt-3 text-text-secondary text-sm">{service.description}</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </button>

            <dialog
              data-service-modal={service.id}
              class="service-modal backdrop:bg-black/70 backdrop:backdrop-blur-sm bg-[#1f1f1f] text-text-primary border-2 border-brand-500 rounded-xl p-0 max-w-2xl w-full shadow-2xl"
            >
              <div class="relative">
                <div class="flex items-start justify-between p-6 border-b border-brand-500/30">
                  <div class="flex items-start gap-4 flex-1">
                    {/* eslint-disable-next-line astro/no-set-html-directive -- Safe: hardcoded static SVG from frontmatter */}
                    <div class="service-icon text-accent flex-shrink-0" set:html={service.icon} />
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold font-coconat text-accent">{service.title}</h3>
                  </div>
                  <button
                    data-modal-close={service.id}
                    class="ml-4 text-text-secondary hover:text-accent transition-colors flex-shrink-0"
                    aria-label="Close dialog"
                  >
                    <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                      <path
                        stroke-linecap="round"
                        stroke-linejoin="round"
                        stroke-width="2"
                        d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12"
                      />
                    </svg>
                  </button>
                </div>
                {/* eslint-disable-next-line astro/no-set-html-directive -- Safe: hardcoded static HTML from frontmatter */}
                <div class="p-6" set:html={service.fullContent} />
              </div>
            </dialog>
          </>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>

  <style>
    .service-card {
      background: linear-gradient(
        135deg,
        rgba(255, 106, 0, 0.08) 0%,
        rgba(255, 106, 0, 0.02) 50%,
        rgba(255, 106, 0, 0.05) 100%
      );
    }

    .service-card:hover {
      background: linear-gradient(
        135deg,
        rgba(255, 106, 0, 0.12) 0%,
        rgba(255, 106, 0, 0.04) 50%,
        rgba(255, 106, 0, 0.08) 100%
      );
      border-left-color: var(--color-brand-400);
      transform: translateX(4px);
      box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(255, 106, 0, 0.15);
    }

    .service-icon {
      padding: 12px;
      background: rgba(255, 106, 0, 0.1);
      border-radius: 12px;
      transition: all 0.3s ease;
    }

    .service-card:hover .service-icon {
      background: rgba(255, 106, 0, 0.2);
      transform: scale(1.05);
    }

    .service-modal {
      margin: auto;
      max-height: 90vh;
      overflow-y: auto;
      color: var(--color-text-primary);
      opacity: 0;
      transform: scale(0.95) translateY(20px);
      transition:
        opacity 0.3s ease-out,
        transform 0.3s ease-out,
        overlay 0.3s ease-out allow-discrete,
        display 0.3s ease-out allow-discrete;
    }

    .service-modal[open] {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: scale(1) translateY(0);
    }

    /* Starting state for @starting-style */
    @starting-style {
      .service-modal[open] {
        opacity: 0;
        transform: scale(0.95) translateY(20px);
      }

      .service-modal[open]::backdrop {
        opacity: 0;
      }
    }

    .service-modal::backdrop {
      backdrop-filter: blur(4px);
      background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7);
      opacity: 0;
      transition:
        opacity 0.3s ease-out,
        backdrop-filter 0.3s ease-out,
        overlay 0.3s ease-out allow-discrete,
        display 0.3s ease-out allow-discrete;
    }

    .service-modal[open]::backdrop {
      opacity: 1;
    }

    /* Ensure modal text colors are correct */
    .service-modal .text-text-primary {
      color: var(--color-text-primary);
    }

    .service-modal .text-text-secondary {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    }

    .service-modal strong {
      color: var(--color-text-primary);
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .service-modal {
        max-width: calc(100vw - 2rem);
      }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    // Modal open handlers
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-service-trigger]').forEach((trigger) => {
      trigger.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const serviceId = trigger.getAttribute('data-service-trigger');
        const modal = document.querySelector(
          `[data-service-modal="${serviceId}"]`
        ) as HTMLDialogElement;
        if (modal) {
          modal.showModal();
          document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
        }
      });
    });

    // Modal close handlers
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-modal-close]').forEach((closeBtn) => {
      closeBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const serviceId = closeBtn.getAttribute('data-modal-close');
        const modal = document.querySelector(
          `[data-service-modal="${serviceId}"]`
        ) as HTMLDialogElement;
        if (modal) {
          modal.close();
          document.body.style.overflow = '';
        }
      });
    });

    // Close on backdrop click
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-service-modal]').forEach((modal) => {
      modal.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        const mouseEvent = e as MouseEvent;
        const dialogElement = modal as HTMLDialogElement;
        const rect = dialogElement.getBoundingClientRect();
        const isInDialog =
          rect.top <= mouseEvent.clientY &&
          mouseEvent.clientY <= rect.top + rect.height &&
          rect.left <= mouseEvent.clientX &&
          mouseEvent.clientX <= rect.left + rect.width;

        if (!isInDialog) {
          dialogElement.close();
          document.body.style.overflow = '';
        }
      });
    });

    // Close on ESC key (native behavior, but also restore scroll)
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-service-modal]').forEach((modal) => {
      modal.addEventListener('close', () => {
        document.body.style.overflow = '';
      });
    });
  </script>
</section>
